  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1216 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nPresent model agreement continues to see a new upper-level trough\npush into the Pacific Northwest early Friday with expectations to\nsee it slowly propagate east across the Northern Rockies and\nNorthern Great Plains this weekend. For us here in the Panhandles\nthis trough will set the stage for better southwesterly flow and\nmonsoonal moisture to return to the Panhandles. Initially on\nFriday, present agreement is not seeing to much activity with us\nhaving to rely on storms pushing of the mountains in Eastern New\nMexico. However as the trough pushes further east over the\nweekend, most models do see our chances become more widespread\nthanks to another passing cold front. Much like the activity last\nnight, these chances will heavily rely on when and how far south\nthe front actually push, which means that present chance of\nshowers can rapidly change over the next 24 hours. Regardless,\npresent agreement has start to favor a more active outlook for\nnext week with some models suggesting a series of upper-level\ntrough push in from the West Coast. Otherwise, look for afternoon\nhighs to stay in upper 80s to mid 90s through Friday, but have the\npotential to cool into the upper 70s to mid 80s with our more\nactive weather this weekend and next week.",
